From 967c3c38b40d4e9032d0d45791c1148d9b76883a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BangerSoul <iamshaikhazmathulla@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] net/rfkill: Export rfkill_set_states for downstream MediaTek Wi-Fi driver

On Lenovo Tab (TB311FU / poplar, MediaTek MT8786 / Helio G85),
the downstream out-of-tree MediaTek Wi-Fi driver (wlan_drv_gen4m_6768.ko)
requires rfkill_set_states() to simultaneously synchronize hardware and software
radio block states during Wi-Fi activation, radio calibration, and airplane mode transitions.

In standard Android Generic Kernel Image (GKI) 6.6 builds, KMI symbol trimming
(CONFIG_TRIM_UNUSED_KSYMS=y) drops unlisted symbols from __ksymtab. Furthermore,
standard upstream kernels do not export rfkill_set_states to loadable modules.
Without this export, loading wlan_drv_gen4m_6768.ko fails with:
  "wlan_drv_gen4m_6768: Unknown symbol rfkill_set_states (err -2)"

Export rfkill_set_states via EXPORT_SYMBOL() and register it in the GKI symbol
whitelist so that downstream vendor connectivity drivers bind cleanly at runtime.

Signed-off-by: Azmathulla Shaik <iamshaikhazmathulla@gmail.com>
---
 android/abi_gki_aarch64 | 1 +
 net/rfkill/core.c       | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/android/abi_gki_aarch64 b/android/abi_gki_aarch64
index 28a1c90..7b91d4e 100644
--- a/android/abi_gki_aarch64
+++ b/android/abi_gki_aarch64
@@ -1045,6 +1045,7 @@
   rfkill_register
   rfkill_resume_polling
   rfkill_set_hw_state
+  rfkill_set_states
   rfkill_set_sw_state
   rfkill_unregister
 diff --git a/net/rfkill/core.c b/net/rfkill/core.c
index 8e3290b21..6d942918a 100644
--- a/net/rfkill/core.c
+++ b/net/rfkill/core.c
@@ -743,6 +743,7 @@ void rfkill_set_states(struct rfkill *rfkill, bool sw, bool hw)
 	rfkill_event(rfkill);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&rfkill->lock, flags);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(rfkill_set_states);
 
 static bool __rfkill_set_hw_state(struct rfkill *rfkill, bool blocked,
 				  bool *change)
